🔋 Company Overview
AI is driving data centre power consumption to more than double — from ~460 TWh today to a projected 1,000 TWh by 2030, roughly the electricity consumption of Japan! Hyperscalers and AI companies are racing to secure compute capacity, while new grid connections in key markets are queued years out. Meanwhile, capacity sits stranded in existing infrastructure — managed through outdated models that were never built to handle the power-dense workloads coming rapidly down the pipe.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Zendo is developing the operating layer that enables operators to get more value from every watt. Our Energy OS platform brings together operational data, energy intelligence, and proprietary load forecasting across the data centre power stack to help operators access more capacity, sooner.&nbsp;
We’ve been building at pace to match the urgency of the capacity crunch, with some great traction so far:&nbsp;

- Raised $2M+ in pre-seed funding from Fly Ventures, Pact, and Octopus Ventures, with angels from Google and across the data centre industry
- Live with several UK data centre customers, with a pipeline to grow across the market
- A founding team combining deep energy, B2B software, and data centre infrastructure expertise — ex-Octopus Energy, Square, Meta
This is an opportunity to join us on the ground floor, work directly with the founders, and grow with the business as we build Zendo into a true category leader on the frontlines of an industry undergoing the largest infrastructure build out in history.&nbsp;


🔎 Your Role as Foundering Operator
You'll work directly with the founders across workstreams spanning from product to energy operations. This is a high-accountability role for someone with energy market experience who acts like a technical product manager — analytical, comfortable in the data, and able to pick up complex problems and drive projects to execution.&nbsp;


Examples of what you'll be working on:

- Managing active PoCs end-to-end with customers — from defining project scopes, objectives, and deliverables through to data collection, on-site logistics and execution
- Identifying opportunities based on customer feedback and operational pain points and translating them into clear product requirements for the engineering team
- Supporting the delivery of energy services to customers through energy data analysis and modelling&nbsp;
- Building out Zendo's energy services methodology and operations — the repeatable processes, templates, and playbooks that underpin how we deliver the best commercial outcomes to customers&nbsp;
- Supporting data analysis and reporting for live customers to drive ongoing value


🌟 What We're Looking For

- 2-4 years of experience in a fast-paced environment (ideally a tech startup) in the energy sector.
- Hands-on experience with energy markets and / or power systems&nbsp;
- Comfortable owning end-to-end delivery — managing PoCs, coordinating stakeholders, and driving projects to completion&nbsp;
- Comfortable working with data — can pull together analysis, interpret results, and present actionable findings clearly&nbsp;
- Tech-lean — you don't need to be an engineer, but you should be comfortable around technical teams and curious about how things work
- Experience with data visualisation in Python, Vibe Coding, Tableau or Power BI
- Highly organised with a bias for action; you don't wait to be told what to do
- Comfortable with ambiguity — we don't have all the answers yet and you should be fine with that


💸 What We're Offering

- A ground-floor role at a well-backed startup at one of the most exciting intersections in tech right now - AI compute and energy&nbsp;
- Work directly with the founders and a growing network of strategic advisors and investors
- A path to a senior or exec role as the company scales
- Access to a lovely co-working space in the heart of London’s Knowledge Quarter
- Quarterly team offsites and socials&nbsp;
- Competitive salary + equity
﻿
📍 Location
Hybrid — we work 1–2 days/week from co-working spaces in London or Newcastle. You must have the legal right to work in the UK (we're not able to sponsor visas).
